## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — Severity-Ranked Findings

This test suite is a textbook example of **"coverage without confidence"** — every production method is invoked (hitting 95% line coverage) but almost nothing is actually *verified*.

---

### 🔴 Critical — Tests That Prove Nothing

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | Bug It Misses |
|---|------|-------------|---------------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` (L17-21) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion at all | `Save()` could silently discard data |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` (L32-36) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion | Price could remain unchanged; nobody checks |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` (L38-43) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion | Product could still exist after delete |
| 4 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L68-74) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion | Discount math could be wrong (e.g., `* fraction` instead of `* (1 - fraction)`) |
| 5 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L84-88) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion | Parsing could corrupt data; fields could be swapped |
| 6 | `GetProductCount_Works` (L63-66) | **Dead variable** — result not asserted | Count could return -1 and the test passes |

**Fix pattern:** Assert the *post-condition*, not just that the method didn't throw.

```csharp
// Example fix for AddProduct_Works
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}
```

---

### 🟠 High — Weak Assertions (Assert-Only-Not-Null)

| # | Test | Problem |
|---|------|---------|
| 7 | `GetProduct_Works` (L28) | Asserts `IsNotNull` but never checks that the *correct* product was returned (Name, Price, Sku) |
| 8 | `SearchProducts_Works` (L51) | Asserts list `IsNotNull` but never checks count or contents — an empty list passes |
| 9 | `GetAllProducts_Works` (L58-59) | Same — `IsNotNull` on a list that could be empty |
| 10 | `ExportToCsv_Works` (L80-81) | `IsNotNull` on a string — `""` or malformed CSV passes fine |

**Fix pattern:** Assert on *values*, not just existence.

```csharp
// Example fix for SearchProducts_Works
[TestMethod]
